  "description": "**Oqtane Marketplace order ingestion, license and trial lifecycle, with customer communications.**\n\n## What it does\n\nAn Oqtane Marketplace order posts to one webhook. License Hub verifies it against a shared secret, stores the order with its license and trial dates, matches the buyer to a CRM contact by email - creating one when the address is new - and publishes the result as CRM webhook events other modules can subscribe to.\n\nThe order list shows every marketplace order with its license, its lifecycle state and the CRM contact it belongs to. License keys are masked in the list and in the detail read; the complete key is behind a manager-only reveal, and reading it is logged.\n\n## Trial lifecycle\n\nTrials are recognised from the license name and given the configured default term when the marketplace sends no expiry date. A trial reports as active, ending soon, expired or past its grace period, computed on UTC boundaries. The warning window, the grace period and the trial length are all module settings.\n\n## Customer communications\n\nThe order is matched to a CRM contact by email address, with optional AI Capture to fill in a name and company. Messages go out through the site's own Oqtane SMTP configuration - License Hub holds no mail server settings of its own.\n\n## Requirements\n\nCustomer messages are wrapped in the CRM email envelope, so every licence mail carries the CRM's corporate identity. Oqtane 10.2.6 and StudioElf CRM 1.6.0 or later. Installing runs one migration that creates the order and communication tables. Five languages: English, Dutch, German, French and Spanish.",
